column36:
Its following CR 27382

1:

{color:#bf2600}The specified fields from Review are locked down for owner {color}

We blocking users to change field in the CR:

Emergency - {{status = Authorize}}

Standard - {{status = Scheduled}}

Non standard - {{status = Authorize}}

the fields:

Assigned to" , "Closure Information" tab and "Actual start date" and Actual end date" These field should be editable for any Fulfiller user (currently is open only for Managers)

The logic should be extended to apply to all statuses from Scheduled onward: Scheduled Implement Review



2:

{color:#bf2600}Able to add CIs to changes in scheduled state after CAB approval. {color}

What happen is that we find that the “Add CI’s” button disappear from the form.

we have fixed that and then we discover other issues.

Now the situation is that, after the CR is- 

Emergency - {{status = Authorize}}

Standard - {{status = Scheduled}}

Non standard - {{status = Authorize}}

The user still able to change the CI and they should NOT be able to.



3:

{color:#ff5630}Unable to add notes to the change {color}

These are internal notes in the change form that should NOT be locked down. 



4:

{color:#ff5630}non relevant RL{color}

The affected CI appear in the form.



5:

{color:#ff5630}Today we blocking the user for all the CR from schedule:{color}

We need blocking users to change field in the CR based on type and status:

Emergency - {{status = Authorize}}

Standard - {{status = Scheduled}}

Non standard - {{status = Authorize}}



