based on the “System Diagnostics” file create a “Playbook” to update the following parameters (in the environment details table”)


1. {color:#4c9aff}Do the client has any patch installed : "patches" section{color}

* {color:#4c9aff}osProps : {color}
*# [{color:#4c9aff}os.name{color}|http://os.name]{color:#4c9aff} - type of OS - Linux or Windows{color}
*# {color:#4c9aff}os.version - OS version they are using {color}
*# {color:#4c9aff}sun.arch.data.model (32/64) {color}
*# {color:#4c9aff}sun.os.patch.level - do they OS have any patches installed on it {color}
*# {color:#4c9aff}user.timezone - OS timezone {color}
* {color:#4c9aff}vmProps - java.version - which Java version customer is using {color}
* {color:#4c9aff}serverProps - server.name.version - web application name and version {color}
* {color:#4c9aff}licenseProps - List of all license attributes customer has {color}
* {color:#4c9aff}acmVersion - ActOne WAR version that is installed{color}
* {color:#4c9aff}dbVersion - ActOne DB version that is installed{color}
* {color:#4c9aff}acmIni : {color}
*# {color:#4c9aff}actimize.jreport.home - tells us if the Jreport is installed or not {color}
*# {color:#4c9aff}actimize.repository.type - tells us which DB type customer is using {color}
* {color:#4c9aff}users - licenseCount - how many named users{color}





